[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Wiki.js has been installed.

  Install layout:
    %%WWWDIR%%                          application source + node_modules
    %%WIKIJS_ETC_DIR%%                  configuration (config.sample.yml here)
    %%WIKIJS_DATA_DIR%%                 runtime data (sqlite db, uploads, etc.)
    %%WIKIJS_LOG_DIR%%                  log files
    %%WIKIJS_RUN_DIR%%                  pidfile

Quick start:

  1.  Copy the sample config and edit it for your database:

        cp %%WIKIJS_ETC_DIR%%/config.sample.yml %%WIKIJS_ETC_DIR%%/config.yml
        $EDITOR %%WIKIJS_ETC_DIR%%/config.yml

      The default config uses SQLite at /var/db/wikijs/data/wiki.sqlite,
      which requires no external services.  Set db.type, db.host, db.user
      etc. for PostgreSQL / MySQL / MariaDB / MSSQL.

  2.  Enable and start the service:

        sysrc wikijs_enable=YES
        service wikijs start

      Optional rc.conf knobs: wikijs_listen_host, wikijs_listen_port,
      wikijs_extra_env, wikijs_extra_args -- see the top of
      %%PREFIX%%/etc/rc.d/wikijs for the full list.

  3.  Browse to http://<server>:3000/ to complete the setup wizard.

  4.  (Recommended) enable log rotation.  Drop this line into
      /etc/newsyslog.conf:

        Include %%PREFIX%%/etc/wikijs/newsyslog.conf.sample

Maintenance:

  Logs:        tail -F %%WIKIJS_LOG_DIR%%/wikijs.log
  Reload:      service wikijs reload   # SIGHUP -- re-read config
  Status:      service wikijs status
  Upgrade:     pkg upgrade wikijs      # rebuilds native modules on FreeBSD

Wiki.js listens on /var/db/wikijs as $WIKIJS_USER.  All runtime data
(uploads, sqlite db, etc.) lives under /var/db/wikijs -- back it up.

EOM
}
]
